1
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:55,500
- Valar morghulis. - Valar dohaeris.

2
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:34,770
I've been sweeping this floor for days.

3
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:39,000
- Good. - I didn't come here to sweep floors.

4
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,350
No? Why come then?

5
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,950
You said that I could be your apprentice.

6
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:48,720
You said you'd teach me how to be a Faceless Man.

7
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,650
A man teaches a girl.

8
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:56,260
Valar dohaeris. All men must serve.

9
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:58,440
Faceless men, most of all.

10
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,310
I want to serve.

11
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:07,910
A girl wants to serve herself.

12
00:04:07,910 --> 00:04:11,460
Here we serve the Many-Faced God. To serve well,

13
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:14,190
a girl must become no-one.

14
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:16,250
Which one is the Many-Faced God?

15
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:19,930
I see the Stranger. I see the Drowned God.

16
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:23,330
- I see the Weirwood Face. - There is only one god.

17
00:04:23,890 --> 00:04:25,630
A girl knows his name.

18
00:04:26,550 --> 00:04:28,370
And all men know his gift.

19
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:07,850
Where are they taking him?

20
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:36,840
Queen Margaery!

21
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:41,810
Queen Margaery!

22
00:05:42,310 --> 00:05:43,840
Queen Margaery!

23
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:51,530
- I am his, and he is mine. - I am hers, and she is mine.

24
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:55,040
From this day until the end of my days.

25
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:40,380
Did I hurt you?

26
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:42,930
No. You were lovely.

27
00:06:43,290 --> 00:06:45,710
- It all happened so fast. - Yes.

28
00:06:46,410 --> 00:06:49,070
I was scared maybe I hurt you. It sounded like...

29
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:50,520
No, no, no...

30
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,650
you're very sweet.

31
00:06:53,130 --> 00:06:55,800
The sweetest king who ever lived.

32
00:06:56,530 --> 00:06:59,220
This is what I want to do all day,

33
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:01,390
every day for the rest of my life.

34
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:03,370
Wouldn't that be glorious?

35
00:07:05,090 --> 00:07:06,870
Shouldn't we rest a little while?

36
00:07:06,870 --> 00:07:09,630
Just to catch our breath. There's no rush, is there?

37
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:10,970
Of course not.

38
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:13,300
Are you hungry?

39
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:16,030
Should I have them bring you some cake or pomegranate juice...?

40
00:07:16,030 --> 00:07:17,270
No, I'm fine...

41
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:20,400
I just want you all to myself.

42
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:23,330
I want to know everything there is to know

43
00:07:23,330 --> 00:07:26,230
about King Tommen, First of His Name.

44
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:30,620
King Tommen... it still sounds strange to me.

45
00:07:31,650 --> 00:07:34,400
Does Queen Margaery sound strange to you?

46
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:36,700
So strange.

47
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:39,790
- Husband. - Wife.

48
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:44,300
Sometimes it feels odd.

49
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:45,970
I'm the king,

50
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:49,930
I've married the most beautiful woman in the world,

51
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:52,880
and it's all because my brother died.

52
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:55,460
I understand.

53
00:07:56,070 --> 00:07:58,890
But it's no your fault. You know that, don't you?

54
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:01,280
You mustn't feel guilty.

55
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,910
I don't feel guilty.

56
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,180
That's what's odd.

57
00:08:09,850 --> 00:08:11,330
Do you like to sail?

58
00:08:11,810 --> 00:08:14,730
- I love to sail. - I do, too.

59
00:08:15,690 --> 00:08:18,520
I think we're going to be very happy, you and I.

60
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:20,440
I do, too.

61
00:08:23,390 --> 00:08:28,050
Living in a tower so high, it touches the clouds.

62
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:32,170
Of course, my grandmother couldn't wait to go home.

63
00:08:32,410 --> 00:08:35,020
The capital is not for everyone, I suppose.

64
00:08:37,230 --> 00:08:39,040
Does your mother like it here?

65
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:41,580
I don't think so.

66
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:44,970
She told me never to trust anyone in King's Landing.

67
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:49,220
It's so wonderful to have her watching over you.

68
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:52,070
A lioness guarding her cub.

69
00:08:52,270 --> 00:08:55,230
Well, but I'm a man now.

70
00:08:57,470 --> 00:08:58,490
You are.

71
00:09:00,730 --> 00:09:02,040
And the king.

72
00:09:04,770 --> 00:09:07,170
But you'll always be her baby-boy.

73
00:09:07,590 --> 00:09:08,810
I suppose.

74
00:09:09,970 --> 00:09:11,500
I adore her. She has always been

75
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,930
so generous with me, so kind.

76
00:09:14,930 --> 00:09:17,310
And the horror she's had to endure -

77
00:09:17,570 --> 00:09:20,710
losing her husband, her eldest child, and her father.

78
00:09:20,710 --> 00:09:23,190
It's no wonder she's so protective of you.

79
00:09:23,530 --> 00:09:26,030
She'll never let you out of her sight.

80
00:09:29,770 --> 00:09:31,490
You look very much in love.

81
00:09:31,710 --> 00:09:34,710
The first days of marriage are often so blissful.

82
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:37,130
She's certainly very pretty, isn't she?

83
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:41,150
Like a doll. She smiles quite a lot.

84
00:09:42,730 --> 00:09:44,720
Do you think she's intelligent?

85
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:47,130
I can't quite tell.

86
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:49,690
Not that it matters.

87
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:51,310
Do you ever miss Casterly Rock?

88
00:09:51,310 --> 00:09:53,580
There's nothing for me in Casterly Rock.

89
00:09:54,370 --> 00:09:55,950
That's where you grew up.

90
00:09:57,810 --> 00:10:00,370
You always told me that you liked the people there better.

91
00:10:00,710 --> 00:10:04,210
You said that King's Landing smelled of horse dung and sour milk.

92
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:09,540
Why are we speaking of Casterly Rock?

93
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:11,220
The way that you talked about it,

94
00:10:11,910 --> 00:10:14,000
I always thought that you missed it,

95
00:10:14,410 --> 00:10:17,170
that you... that it was your real home.

96
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:19,030
This is my real home now.

97
00:10:19,030 --> 00:10:20,780
Where my family lives.

98
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:24,010
I want you to be happy, mother.

99
00:10:24,850 --> 00:10:26,140
I know that.

100
00:10:27,690 --> 00:10:30,530
I know you do. My sweet boy.

101
00:10:30,610 --> 00:10:32,960
But wouldn't you be happier in Casterly Rock?

102
00:10:35,330 --> 00:10:38,920
I said, "Darling, surely four times is enough."

103
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,770
"Are you trying to set a new record?"

104
00:10:40,770 --> 00:10:43,220
And he said, "Well, what is the record?

105
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:44,950
I'm sure we can break it."

106
00:10:49,930 --> 00:10:51,150
Mother.

107
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,330
Welcome.

108
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:55,940
Don't you look lovely.

109
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,380
Marriage agrees with you.

110
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:00,090
Can we bring you anything to eat or drink?

111
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,660
I wish we had some wine for you.

112
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:03,680
It's a bit early in the day for us.

113
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:08,000
No, no, I... I can't stay.

114
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:11,000
I just wanted to let you know

115
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:13,380
if there's ever anything I can do for you.

116
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:14,980
You are very sweet.

117
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:17,760
Tommen seems quite taken with his new queen.

118
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,790
I absolutely adore him.

119
00:11:20,790 --> 00:11:22,570
You raised a gallant young man.

120
00:11:22,570 --> 00:11:25,060
- I'm forever grateful. - Good.

121
00:11:26,590 --> 00:11:27,670
Good.

122
00:11:27,910 --> 00:11:29,110
I'm glad to hear you're happy.

123
00:11:29,110 --> 00:11:31,400
Ecstatic. I really am.

124
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:34,250
Exhausted, to be honest, but

125
00:11:34,310 --> 00:11:37,660
what can I expect, he is half lion, half stag.

126
00:11:39,540 --> 00:11:41,110
I'll leave you to it then.

127
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,790
Oh, forgive me,

128
00:11:42,790 --> 00:11:44,480
I haven't been at Court for long,

129
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:46,080
I get so confused.

130
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,320
What's the proper way to address you now?

131
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:50,600
Queen Mother or Dowager Queen?

132
00:11:52,490 --> 00:11:54,440
There's no need for such formalities.

133
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:57,790
In any event, judging from the King's enthusiasm,

134
00:11:57,790 --> 00:12:00,270
the Queen Mother will be a Queen Grandmother soon.

135
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,760
Won't that be a lovely day.

136
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,650
Can you imagine the celebrations?

137
00:12:03,650 --> 00:12:06,020
They'll ring the bells all day and night.

138
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:07,130
Remember.

139
00:12:08,630 --> 00:12:10,190
Anything you need.

140
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:27,970
We can't hold the North with terror alone.

141
00:13:27,970 --> 00:13:30,930
You can't hold the North if you let these lesser lords insult us.

142
00:13:30,930 --> 00:13:33,700
I sent you there to collect taxes, not bodies.

143
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,470
Lord Cerwyn refused to pay.

144
00:13:36,510 --> 00:13:38,960
He said the Warden of the North would always be a Stark

145
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:41,600
and he'd be damned if he'd kiss a traitor's boot.

146
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,710
He left you no choice.

147
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:47,760
I flayed him living,

148
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:50,060
along with his wife and brother.

149
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:52,010
I made his son watch.

150
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:54,700
And?

151
00:13:54,890 --> 00:13:57,200
The new Lord Cerwyn paid his taxes.

152
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:06,030
I have something important to tell you.

153
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:09,230
Stop eating and listen.

154
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:20,500
We don't have enough men to hold the North

155
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,820
if the other Houses rise up against us.

156
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,570
Do you understand that?

157
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:26,450
Our pact with the Lannisters protects...

158
00:14:26,450 --> 00:14:28,350
I had a pact with Tywin Lannister.

159
00:14:28,350 --> 00:14:30,140
And Tywin Lannister is dead.

160
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,940
The remaining Lannisters are a thousand miles away

161
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:34,280
dealing with that fact.

162
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:36,580
They've never once in the history of the Seven Kingdoms

163
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:38,510
sent their army this far north.

164
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:41,340
If you think they will for us, you're a fool.

165
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:44,080
We've  become a great House

166
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,360
by entering into alliances with other Houses,

167
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,450
and parlaying those alliances into greater power.

168
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:52,170
The best way to forge a lasting alliance

169
00:14:52,170 --> 00:14:54,550
isn't by peeling a man's skin off.

170
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:56,820
The best way is marriage.

171
00:14:57,730 --> 00:15:00,430
Now that you're a Bolton by royal decree,

172
00:15:01,030 --> 00:15:03,430
it's high time you married a suitable bride.

173
00:15:07,330 --> 00:15:08,710
And as it happens,

174
00:15:09,050 --> 00:15:12,680
I've found the perfect girl to solidify our hold on the North.

175
00:15:34,660 --> 00:15:36,990
- That's Moat Cailin. - Yes.

176
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:39,040
A bit shabby, isn't it?

177
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:41,200
You've been here before.

178
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,450
On our way down to King's Landing,

179
00:15:43,450 --> 00:15:45,740
with my father and Arya and...

180
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:49,180
- Where are you taking me? - Home.

181
00:15:51,410 --> 00:15:53,400
The Boltons have Winterfell.

182
00:15:56,870 --> 00:15:59,450
Your marriage proposal, it wasn't for you?

183
00:16:00,870 --> 00:16:01,950
No.

184
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:05,510
Roose Bolton murdered my brother.

185
00:16:05,510 --> 00:16:07,310
He betrayed my family!

186
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:08,410
He did.

187
00:16:08,810 --> 00:16:10,870
He serves the Lannisters.

188
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:13,350
- For now. - I won't go.

189
00:16:13,450 --> 00:16:15,760
- Winterfell is your home. - Not anymore.

190
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:18,440
Always. You're a Stark.

191
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:21,750
Dying your hair doesn't change that. You're Sansa Stark.

192
00:16:21,750 --> 00:16:24,680
The eldest surviving child of Ned and Catelyn Stark.

193
00:16:25,130 --> 00:16:26,690
Your place is in the North.

194
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:28,650
I can't marry him. You can't make me.

195
00:16:28,650 --> 00:16:30,980
He is a traitor. A murderer!

196
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:32,870
You're not marrying Roose Bolton.

197
00:16:32,870 --> 00:16:36,230
No, you'll be marrying his son and heir, Ramsay.

198
00:16:36,460 --> 00:16:39,040
- One day he'll be Warden of the North and you... - No!

199
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:40,870
- Sansa... - No, you can't make me.

200
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:42,190
I will starve myself.

201
00:16:42,190 --> 00:16:44,540
I will die before I have to go there.

202
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:46,740
I won't force you to do anything.

203
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:49,890
Don't you know by now how much I care for you?

204
00:16:51,250 --> 00:16:53,900
Say the word and we turn the horses round, but listen to me.

205
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,030
Listen.

206
00:16:55,650 --> 00:16:57,520
You've been running all your life.

207
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:01,680
Terrible things happened to your family and you weep.

208
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:04,790
You sit alone in a darkened room, mourning their fates.

209
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:06,450
You've been a bystander to tragedy

210
00:17:06,450 --> 00:17:08,790
from the day they executed your father.

211
00:17:09,490 --> 00:17:12,010
Stop being a bystander. You hear me?

212
00:17:12,010 --> 00:17:13,180
Stop running.

213
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:20,460
There's no justice in the world.

214
00:17:21,310 --> 00:17:22,960
Not unless we make it.

215
00:17:24,810 --> 00:17:26,290
You loved your family.

216
00:17:28,210 --> 00:17:29,480
Avenge them.

217
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,420
How do we get through there?

218
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:33,950
We don't.

219
00:18:34,250 --> 00:18:35,520
We go around.

220
00:18:35,910 --> 00:18:37,530
Takes us miles out of the way.

221
00:18:38,550 --> 00:18:41,040
- We'll lose sight of them. - Doesn't matter.

222
00:18:41,090 --> 00:18:42,420
I know where they're going.

223
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:48,730
Are you getting a bit old to be a squire?

224
00:18:53,510 --> 00:18:55,900
How did you end up squiring for the Imp?

225
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:57,670
He hates that nickname.

226
00:18:57,670 --> 00:19:00,090
Well, he's not here to complain about it, is he?

227
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:06,020
I squired for a knight named Ser Lorimer

228
00:19:06,030 --> 00:19:08,180
during the War of the Five Kings.

229
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:09,510
One night,

230
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:11,320
he had a bit too much to drink

231
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:14,000
and he was famished, so he borrowed a ham.

232
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,590
- He borrowed it? - He wasn't a thief.

233
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:19,220
He was drunk and hungry and he wasn't thinking.

234
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:20,520
I was drunk too.

235
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,960
He gave me half the ham.

236
00:19:24,690 --> 00:19:25,940
Next morning,

237
00:19:26,430 --> 00:19:28,880
one of the guards saw him passed out

238
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:31,870
under a wagon with the ham bone still in his hand.

239
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:34,520
They hanged the man after noon.

240
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:37,680
They tied the noose for me too,

241
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:40,180
but Lord Tywin heard my family name was Payne,

242
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:41,680
so he pardoned me,

243
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:44,270
and sent me to King's Landing to squire for his son.

244
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:45,790
As punishment

245
00:19:46,550 --> 00:19:49,210
- for both of you. - It didn't seem that way.

246
00:19:49,650 --> 00:19:51,680
Lord Tyrion was always very good to me.

247
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,830
Yes, all of your lords have been very kind to you.

248
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:55,320
All except me.

249
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:58,220
Sorry you had to squire for such a nasty person.

250
00:19:58,220 --> 00:20:00,910
I'm not sorry. You're the best fighter I've ever seen.

251
00:20:01,260 --> 00:20:02,780
You beat The Hound.

252
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:05,780
I'm proud to be your squire.

253
00:20:10,850 --> 00:20:13,010
I'm sorry I'm always snapping at you.

254
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:15,480
If you didn't snap at me, I wouldn't learn anything.

255
00:20:19,540 --> 00:20:21,150
You want to be a knight, Pod?

256
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:23,650
Yes.

257
00:20:23,650 --> 00:20:26,390
Starting tomorrow, we'll train with the sword twice a day,

258
00:20:26,390 --> 00:20:29,460
before we ride in the morning and after you make camp in the evening.

259
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:32,240
And I'm going to show you how to ride properly.

260
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,030
Thank you.

261
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,270
I can't knight you,

262
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:35,730
but I can teach you how to fight.

263
00:20:35,730 --> 00:20:37,550
I suppose that's more important.

264
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,770
You weren't a knight, but

265
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:55,120
you were a Kingsguard to Renly Baratheon, weren't you?

266
00:20:56,060 --> 00:20:57,040
I was.

267
00:20:57,710 --> 00:20:59,800
Lord Tyrion said he was a good man.

268
00:21:02,130 --> 00:21:03,140
He was.

269
00:21:05,130 --> 00:21:07,130
How did you end up serving Renly?

270
00:21:13,330 --> 00:21:14,260
When I was a girl,

271
00:21:14,260 --> 00:21:16,220
my father held a ball.

272
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:17,600
I'm his only living child,

273
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:19,730
so he wanted to make a good match for me.

274
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:22,440
He invited dozens of young lords to Tarth.

275
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:25,560
I didn't want to go, but he dragged me to the ballroom.

276
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:30,310
And it was wonderful.

277
00:21:32,670 --> 00:21:36,320
None of the boys noticed how mulish and tall I was.

278
00:21:37,350 --> 00:21:39,690
They shove each other and threatened to duel

279
00:21:39,690 --> 00:21:41,910
when they thought it was their turn to dance.

280
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:44,780
Whispered in my ear

281
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:46,580
how they wanted to marry me

282
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:48,830
and take me back to their castles.

283
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:54,200
My father smiled at me and I smiled at him.

284
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:58,040
I had never been so happy.

285
00:22:01,350 --> 00:22:03,860
Till I saw a few of the boys snickering.

286
00:22:05,860 --> 00:22:07,550
And then they all started to laugh,

287
00:22:07,550 --> 00:22:09,590
they couldn't keep the game going any longer.

288
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:12,110
They were toying with me.

289
00:22:13,490 --> 00:22:15,830
"Brienne the Beauty" they called me.

290
00:22:15,830 --> 00:22:17,340
Great joke.

291
00:22:18,660 --> 00:22:22,350
And I realized I was the ugliest girl alive.

292
00:22:23,260 --> 00:22:26,050
A great lumbering beast.

293
00:22:30,790 --> 00:22:31,920
I tried to run away,

294
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:34,740
but Renly Baratheon took me in his arms.

295
00:22:35,530 --> 00:22:38,140
"Don't let them see your tears", he told me.

296
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:40,240
"The nasty little shits

297
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:43,110
and nasty little shits aren't worth crying over."

298
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:47,510
He danced with me and none of the other boys could say a word.

299
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:51,230
Renly was the king's brother after all.

300
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:55,370
But wasn't he...

301
00:22:57,320 --> 00:22:59,600
Lord Tyrion said he was...

302
00:23:00,990 --> 00:23:04,010
Yes, Pod, he liked men. I'm not an idiot.

303
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:05,880
He didn't love me. He didn't want me,

304
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:07,680
he danced with me because he was kind

305
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:09,470
and he didn't want to see me hurt.

306
00:23:10,330 --> 00:23:13,270
He saved me from being a joke.

307
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:14,820
From that day

308
00:23:15,190 --> 00:23:16,930
until his last day.

309
00:23:19,660 --> 00:23:22,010
And I couldn't save him in return.

310
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:27,700
Nothing's more hateful than failing to protect

311
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:29,160
the one you love.

312
00:23:31,380 --> 00:23:34,010
One day, I will avenge King Renly.

313
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:36,390
But you said a shadow murdered him.

314
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:38,930
How do you fight a shadow?

315
00:23:38,930 --> 00:23:41,930
A shadow with the face of Stannis Baratheon.

316
00:23:42,790 --> 00:23:44,230
I know it was Stannis.

317
00:23:44,230 --> 00:23:45,980
I know it in my heart.

318
00:23:49,470 --> 00:23:51,820
Stannis is a man, not a shadow.

319
00:23:52,630 --> 00:23:53,870
And a man

320
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:56,280
can be killed.

321
00:23:59,190 --> 00:24:01,030
- Lord Commander. - Your Grace.

322
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:02,880
I'd like to speak alone.

323
00:24:03,330 --> 00:24:05,110
Olly is my steward now,

324
00:24:05,630 --> 00:24:07,650
as I was Lord Commander Mormont's.

325
00:24:08,570 --> 00:24:10,410
I want him to attend my meetings,

326
00:24:10,450 --> 00:24:12,920
to learn from men with experience.

327
00:24:14,530 --> 00:24:16,430
One day, he might command.

328
00:24:20,390 --> 00:24:23,130
Very well. Have you considered my offer?

329
00:24:24,930 --> 00:24:25,950
I have.

330
00:24:26,140 --> 00:24:28,540
And I thank you for it. You do me great honor.

331
00:24:29,540 --> 00:24:32,130
All my life I wanted to be Jon Stark.

332
00:24:32,130 --> 00:24:33,550
Say the word and you will be.

333
00:24:35,580 --> 00:24:37,500
But I have to refuse you.

334
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:41,200
I'm Lord Commander of the Night's Watch.

335
00:24:41,510 --> 00:24:42,950
My place is here.

336
00:24:42,950 --> 00:24:45,680
I'm giving you the chance to avenge your family,

337
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:49,200
to take back the castle where you grew up,

338
00:24:51,460 --> 00:24:53,370
to rule the North.

339
00:24:53,540 --> 00:24:55,390
I wish I could fight beside you.

340
00:24:56,180 --> 00:24:57,910
Believe me, I do.

341
00:24:58,170 --> 00:25:01,280
But I swore a sacred vow at the Godswood.

342
00:25:01,620 --> 00:25:04,380
I pledged my life to the Night's Watch.

343
00:25:04,380 --> 00:25:06,460
You're as stubborn as your father.

344
00:25:07,670 --> 00:25:09,080
And as honorable.

345
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:11,020
I can imagine no higher praise.

346
00:25:11,020 --> 00:25:12,740
I didn't mean it as praise.

347
00:25:12,750 --> 00:25:14,720
Honor got your father killed.

348
00:25:15,220 --> 00:25:16,110
But if your mind's made up,

349
00:25:16,110 --> 00:25:17,440
I won't try and dissuade you.

350
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:18,860
May I ask, Your Grace,

351
00:25:18,860 --> 00:25:20,730
how long you plan to stay at Castle Black?

352
00:25:20,730 --> 00:25:22,380
Are you bored of us already?

353
00:25:23,890 --> 00:25:26,080
You saved us from Mance Rayder's army.

354
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:27,690
We will never forget that.

355
00:25:27,830 --> 00:25:29,680
But it's a question of survival.

356
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:31,710
The Night's Watch can't continue to

357
00:25:31,710 --> 00:25:34,880
feed your men and the wildling prisoners indefinitely.

358
00:25:35,310 --> 00:25:37,380
Winter is coming.

359
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:40,230
I know it.

360
00:25:40,430 --> 00:25:42,770
We march on Winterfell within the fortnight,

361
00:25:42,770 --> 00:25:44,710
before the snows trap us here.

362
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:47,310
And the wildlings?

363
00:25:47,310 --> 00:25:49,230
If they'd rather burn than fight for me,

364
00:25:49,230 --> 00:25:49,770
so be it.

365
00:25:49,770 --> 00:25:51,390
I leave their fate to you.

366
00:25:52,020 --> 00:25:54,880
You could execute them. That's the safest course.

367
00:25:59,150 --> 00:26:01,550
Or you could see if this Tormund fellow is more willing

368
00:26:01,550 --> 00:26:03,730
to compromise than Mance ever was.

369
00:26:03,730 --> 00:26:04,640
I assume the brothers of

370
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:07,200
the Night's Watch would rather see the wildlings dead.

371
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:08,950
Most of the brothers, yes.

372
00:26:10,190 --> 00:26:12,390
There's little love for the free folk here.

373
00:26:12,850 --> 00:26:14,500
You're the Lord Commander.

374
00:26:14,710 --> 00:26:16,010
Your decision.

375
00:26:18,010 --> 00:26:19,780
You have many enemies in Castle Black.

376
00:26:19,780 --> 00:26:22,650
Have you considered sending Alliser Thorne elsewhere?

377
00:26:24,130 --> 00:26:26,560
Give him command of Eastwach by the Sea.

378
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:29,360
I heard it was best to keep your enemies close.

379
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:31,440
Whoever said that didn't have many enemies.

380
00:26:39,560 --> 00:26:41,110
He sees something in you.

381
00:26:42,780 --> 00:26:44,960
Might not be apparent from his tone,

382
00:26:45,750 --> 00:26:47,940
but it's the truth. He believes in you.

383
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:49,870
I'm sorry I disappointed him.

384
00:26:54,510 --> 00:26:56,990
The king is a complicated man,

385
00:26:57,810 --> 00:27:00,320
but he wants what's right for the Seven Kingdoms.

386
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:01,760
As long as he's ruling them.

387
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,310
He's the one true king.

388
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:06,270
He has a blood right to that throne.

389
00:27:06,270 --> 00:27:09,960
I've sworn to stay clear of the politics of the Seven Kingdoms.

390
00:27:09,970 --> 00:27:11,150
Have you now?

391
00:27:14,380 --> 00:27:16,620
How does the Night's Watch vow go again?

392
00:27:17,250 --> 00:27:19,420
I'll bet you've got it memorized since you got here.

393
00:27:22,360 --> 00:27:24,720
Night gathers and now my watch begins...

394
00:27:24,720 --> 00:27:27,330
Not that bit, the bit at the end.

395
00:27:28,210 --> 00:27:30,600
I'm the sword in the darkness,

396
00:27:30,700 --> 00:27:32,420
the watcher on the walls,

397
00:27:32,420 --> 00:27:34,970
the shield that guards the realm of men.

398
00:27:34,970 --> 00:27:36,770
- I pledge my life... - Right, that's enough.

399
00:27:36,770 --> 00:27:39,060
The shield that guards the realm of men.

400
00:27:39,990 --> 00:27:41,590
That's what you swore to be.

401
00:27:41,830 --> 00:27:43,290
Now, I'm not a learned man,

402
00:27:43,290 --> 00:27:45,490
but the best way to help the most people might not be sitting

403
00:27:45,500 --> 00:27:48,210
in a frozen castle at the edge of the world.

404
00:27:48,210 --> 00:27:50,570
It just might mean wading in the muck,

405
00:27:50,570 --> 00:27:53,760
getting your boots dirty, and doing what needs to be done.

406
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:55,300
And what needs to be done?

407
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:57,400
As long as the Boltons rule the North,

408
00:27:57,930 --> 00:27:59,500
the North will suffer.

409
00:28:00,490 --> 00:28:01,980
Just one man's opinion.

410
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:32,790
What do you want?

411
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:34,930
Who are you?

412
00:28:36,610 --> 00:28:37,380
What?

413
00:28:37,430 --> 00:28:40,330
You, who walk in here with a coin you never earned,

414
00:28:40,330 --> 00:28:42,410
whose value you do not respect.

415
00:28:48,550 --> 00:28:49,470
Who are you?

416
00:28:52,560 --> 00:28:53,420
No one.

417
00:28:53,720 --> 00:28:55,280
Ou! Cunt!

418
00:28:55,280 --> 00:28:57,320
A lie. A sad little lie.

419
00:28:57,660 --> 00:28:59,360
- Who are you? - I told you, I'm no...

420
00:28:59,880 --> 00:29:01,020
Do that again and...

421
00:29:02,310 --> 00:29:03,360
Who are you?

422
00:29:04,250 --> 00:29:05,650
You're about to find out.

423
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:08,380
What are you doing?

424
00:29:09,120 --> 00:29:10,230
We were only playing.

425
00:29:10,590 --> 00:29:11,930
The Game of Faces.

426
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:13,480
That girl is not ready.

427
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:14,610
Clearly not.

428
00:29:14,740 --> 00:29:15,920
I am ready.

429
00:29:17,750 --> 00:29:18,940
For what?

430
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,270
For every you want,

431
00:29:20,270 --> 00:29:22,190
to be a Faceless Man,

432
00:29:22,190 --> 00:29:23,320
to be no one.

433
00:29:28,190 --> 00:29:29,610
Whose sword is that?

434
00:29:29,940 --> 00:29:31,650
It belongs to Arya Stark.

435
00:29:31,650 --> 00:29:33,970
Arya Stark's sword, Arya Stark's clothes,

436
00:29:33,970 --> 00:29:35,940
Arya Stark's stolen silver.

437
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:37,720
A man wonders

438
00:29:38,110 --> 00:29:40,230
how is it that no one

439
00:29:40,380 --> 00:29:43,410
came to be surrounded by Arya Stark's things?

440
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:50,260
What do we do with them after we wash them?

441
00:34:21,530 --> 00:34:23,340
Open gates!

442
00:34:55,810 --> 00:34:58,670
Lady Sansa. Welcome.

443
00:35:05,200 --> 00:35:06,240
Lord Bolton.

444
00:35:08,260 --> 00:35:12,010
May I introduce my son, Ramsay Bolton?

445
00:35:14,710 --> 00:35:17,820
It's an honor to meet you, my lady.

446
00:35:33,320 --> 00:35:35,480
I'll bring you a bowl of hot water.

447
00:35:35,810 --> 00:35:37,340
You must want to wash.

448
00:35:38,430 --> 00:35:39,510
Thank you.

449
00:35:42,930 --> 00:35:44,780
Welcome home, Lady Stark.

450
00:35:47,200 --> 00:35:48,790
The North remembers.

451
00:36:02,380 --> 00:36:03,110
Sam?

452
00:36:04,870 --> 00:36:05,960
Maester Aemon?

453
00:36:06,090 --> 00:36:08,160
He apologizes for not being here.

454
00:36:09,190 --> 00:36:10,470
He's not feeling well.

455
00:36:10,720 --> 00:36:12,010
Take good care of him.

456
00:36:12,670 --> 00:36:14,080
I will drink it then.

457
00:36:14,130 --> 00:36:15,070
Brothers.

458
00:36:16,520 --> 00:36:17,930
As you all know too well,

459
00:36:17,940 --> 00:36:20,420
it's long past time to dig a new latrine pit.

460
00:36:24,620 --> 00:36:26,770
First Builder Yarwyck and I have decided to appoint

461
00:36:26,770 --> 00:36:30,130
a latrine captain to oversee this crucial task.

462
00:36:37,480 --> 00:36:38,290
Brian.

463
00:36:39,250 --> 00:36:41,030
It seems like a good job for a ginger.

464
00:36:48,980 --> 00:36:50,030
Ser Alliser.

465
00:36:54,180 --> 00:36:57,370
You have more experience than any other ranger at Castle Black.

466
00:36:57,530 --> 00:36:59,780
You proved your valour many times over

467
00:36:59,900 --> 00:37:02,380
by defending the Wall from the wildling attack.

468
00:37:05,390 --> 00:37:07,080
I name you First Ranger.

469
00:37:14,230 --> 00:37:15,200
Lord Janos.

470
00:37:15,930 --> 00:37:17,710
I'm giving you command of Greyguard.

471
00:37:19,380 --> 00:37:20,580
Greyguard is a ruin.

472
00:37:20,580 --> 00:37:22,810
Yes, the fort is in a sorry state.

473
00:37:22,860 --> 00:37:24,430
Restore it as best you can.

474
00:37:24,670 --> 00:37:26,120
First Builder Yarwyck can spare 10 of his...

475
00:37:26,120 --> 00:37:28,200
I was charged with the defense of King's Landing

476
00:37:28,210 --> 00:37:30,350
when you were soiling your swaddling clothes.

477
00:37:30,350 --> 00:37:31,750
Keep your ruin.

478
00:37:35,310 --> 00:37:36,780
Alright, alright.

479
00:37:36,900 --> 00:37:38,150
Enough of that.

480
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:40,390
You mistake me, my Lord.

481
00:37:42,320 --> 00:37:45,040
That was a command, not an offer.

482
00:37:45,300 --> 00:37:48,290
Pack your arms and armour, say your farewells,

483
00:37:49,220 --> 00:37:50,750
and ride for Greyguard.

484
00:37:53,630 --> 00:37:56,370
I will not go meekly off to freeze and die.

485
00:37:56,650 --> 00:37:59,410
Give it to one of the fools who cast a stone for you.

486
00:37:59,650 --> 00:38:00,900
I will not have it.

487
00:38:00,900 --> 00:38:02,230
Did you hear me, boy?

488
00:38:02,230 --> 00:38:04,060
I will not have it!

489
00:38:04,400 --> 00:38:06,560
You refusing to obey my order?

490
00:38:12,410 --> 00:38:15,450
You can stick your order up your bastard arse.

491
00:38:22,910 --> 00:38:24,630
Take Lord Janos outside.

492
00:38:27,070 --> 00:38:28,610
Olly, bring me my sword.

493
00:38:50,970 --> 00:38:52,470
You cannot do this!

494
00:38:52,550 --> 00:38:53,790
Get your hands off me!

495
00:38:54,350 --> 00:38:56,110
Scum! All of you!

496
00:39:00,600 --> 00:39:02,610
If the boy thinks he can frighten me,

497
00:39:02,610 --> 00:39:05,210
je's mistaken, yes, very mistaken.

498
00:39:07,350 --> 00:39:09,150
Disgrace!

499
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:12,090
I have friends. Important friends in the capital!

500
00:39:12,090 --> 00:39:13,150
You'll see!

501
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:51,380
If you have any last words, my Lord,

502
00:39:52,460 --> 00:39:53,540
now is the time.

503
00:39:56,910 --> 00:39:59,200
I was wrong. You're the Lord Commander!

504
00:39:59,200 --> 00:40:01,270
We all serve you. I'm sorry.

505
00:40:01,270 --> 00:40:03,900
Not only for this, for all I've done and said.

506
00:40:05,890 --> 00:40:06,800
I was wrong!

507
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:11,740
My Lord, please, mercy! Mercy!

508
00:40:12,120 --> 00:40:13,360
I'll go! I will!

509
00:40:14,270 --> 00:40:15,360
Please.

510
00:40:16,190 --> 00:40:17,300
I'm afraid.

511
00:40:19,110 --> 00:40:21,410
I've always been afraid.

512
00:41:05,260 --> 00:41:08,600
You have served us well, my son.

513
00:41:08,650 --> 00:41:10,020
Thank you, Father!

514
00:41:10,160 --> 00:41:13,070
Which of the Seven will you worship today?

515
00:41:13,080 --> 00:41:16,270
- The Maiden... - Always the Maiden

516
00:41:17,460 --> 00:41:19,250
And the Stranger.

517
00:41:19,450 --> 00:41:22,200
- Two is extra, you realize... - Yes, yes.

518
00:41:33,900 --> 00:41:34,890
What are you doing?

519
00:41:35,230 --> 00:41:38,160
This establishment belong to Lord Petyr Baelish. You can't...

520
00:41:39,070 --> 00:41:41,130
You have profaned our Faith.

521
00:41:41,130 --> 00:41:43,970
The Faith of our fathers and forefathers.

522
00:41:43,980 --> 00:41:46,080
I am the High Septon of the...

523
00:41:46,080 --> 00:41:47,760
You are a sinner.

524
00:41:48,420 --> 00:41:50,050
And you shall be punished.

525
00:42:04,850 --> 00:42:06,490
Sinner! Sinner!

526
00:42:07,170 --> 00:42:08,780
- Sinner! - Repent!

527
00:42:08,780 --> 00:42:10,620
Sinner! Sinner!

528
00:42:10,620 --> 00:42:12,780
Sinner! Sinner! Sinner!

529
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:16,340
- Sinner! Sinner! - Shame on you!

530
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:17,720
Sinner!

531
00:42:28,550 --> 00:42:31,320
Your Grace, Grandmaester, Lord Tyrell...

532
00:42:33,240 --> 00:42:34,440
It doesn't matter.

533
00:42:35,910 --> 00:42:38,060
As the High Septon of the Faith of the Seven

534
00:42:38,060 --> 00:42:39,720
I give voice to the will of the Gods

535
00:42:39,720 --> 00:42:42,860
and I am their foremost servant in this world.

536
00:42:43,100 --> 00:42:46,060
An insult to me is an insult to the Gods.

537
00:42:46,070 --> 00:42:48,480
An assault on my person

538
00:42:48,680 --> 00:42:50,420
is an assault on our very religion.

539
00:42:50,430 --> 00:42:51,380
You were assaulted?

540
